<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muammar Gaddafi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a>–<a href="/years/2011">2011</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Colonel Gaddafi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muammar Gaddafi was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> from 1969 to 2011. A young army officer, he led the coup of 1 September 1969 that overthrew King Idris and set up a revolutionary republic, later called the Jamahiriya, based on the ideas of his Green Book. He nationalised oil, backed militant movements abroad and faced international <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>; he was overthrown in the 2011 civil war and killed near Sirte.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muammar-gaddafi.jpg" alt="Muammar Gaddafi" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stevan Kragujević · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moamer_el_Gadafi_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
